From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xhci-aeolia: bring up the fat PS4's internal hard drive again

On the fat PS4 (Aeolia) the internal hard drive is a USB-SATA bridge on the
middle xHCI host controller. With this kernel it never answers ("usb 4-1:
device descriptor read/8, error -110"), so Linux sees no internal drive
(ps4-multiboot issue #3, EmuFive issue #38). The 7.0 kernel found it.

Do what the 7.0 driver did on Aeolia: pause before each host controller
comes up (7.0 had the pause from console printk calls), no interrupt
moderation, and no USB streams, so the bridge uses usb-storage as before.
Belize and Baikal are unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-aeolia.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-aeolia.c
index d3a5834c6..51ee5a938 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-aeolia.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-aeolia.c
@@ -50,6 +50,10 @@ static void xhci_aeolia_quirks(struct device *dev, struct xhci_hcd *xhci)
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_PLAT;
 		xhci->imod_interval = 0;
 	}
+
+	/* Aeolia (fat PS4): no interrupt moderation, as in the 7.0 kernel. */
+	if (to_pci_dev(dev)->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_SONY_AEOLIA_XHCI)
+		xhci->imod_interval = 0;
 }
 
 /* called during probe() after chip reset completes */
@@ -99,7 +103,16 @@ static int xhci_aeolia_probe_one(struct pci_dev *dev, int index)
 			 index, dev->device, irq);
 	else
 		dev_dbg(&dev->dev, "xhci_aeolia_probe_one %d\n", index);
-	usleep_range(200, 500);
+	/*
+	 * Aeolia's middle host controller carries the internal hard drive (a
+	 * USB-SATA bridge). It only came up after a pause: the 7.0 kernel had one
+	 * from its console printk calls here and in the MSI setup, and without it
+	 * the bridge never answers (device descriptor read, error -110).
+	 */
+	if (xhci_aeolia_has_middle_host(dev))
+		msleep(50);
+	else
+		usleep_range(200, 500);
 
 	hcd = usb_create_hcd(driver, &dev->dev, pci_name(dev));
 	pci_set_drvdata(dev, axhci); /* usb_create_hcd clobbers this */
@@ -137,7 +150,8 @@ static int xhci_aeolia_probe_one(struct pci_dev *dev, int index)
 	if (retval)
 		goto put_usb3_hcd;
 
-	if (!xhci_aeolia_is_baikal(dev)) {
+	/* Not on Aeolia: its hard drive bridge ran with usb-storage, not UAS streams. */
+	if (dev->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_SONY_BELIZE_XHCI) {
 		struct usb_hcd *usb3_hcd = xhci_get_usb3_hcd(xhci);
 
 		if (usb3_hcd && GET_MAX_PSA_SIZE(xhci->hcc_params) >= 4 &&
